A login route builds its query like this. What is the correct fix?

```js
const sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '" + req.body.email + "'";
const { rows } = await db.query(sql);
```

An endpoint creates thumbnails. What is the safest change?

```js
const { exec } = require('node:child_process');
exec(`convert uploads/${req.query.file} -resize 200x200 thumbs/out.png`);
```

An Express API using MongoDB has this login check. An attacker sends the JSON body `{"user":"admin","password":{"$ne":null}}`. What happens, and what is the fix?

```js
app.post('/login', express.json(), async (req, res) => {
  const u = await users.findOne({ user: req.body.user, password: req.body.password });
  if (u) return res.send('welcome');
  res.status(401).end();
});
```

A download route serves files from `/srv/files`. What does a request for `?name=../../etc/passwd` read?

```js
app.get('/download', (req, res) => {
  const full = path.join('/srv/files', req.query.name);
  res.sendFile(full);
});
```

A settings endpoint deep-merges the request body into a defaults object with this function. A client sends `{"__proto__": {"isAdmin": true}}`. What does `({}).isAdmin` evaluate to afterwards, anywhere in the process?

```js
function merge(target, src) {
  for (const key in src) {
    if (typeof src[key] === 'object' && src[key] !== null) {
      if (!target[key]) target[key] = {};
      merge(target[key], src[key]);
    } else {
      target[key] = src[key];
    }
  }
  return target;
}
merge(defaults, JSON.parse(body));
```

An API that uses cookie sessions sets these CORS headers on every response. What is the risk?

```js
res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', req.headers.origin);
res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true');
```

A team "fixed" path traversal with this check. Which request still reads a file outside `/srv/files`?

```js
const base = '/srv/files';
const full = path.resolve(base, req.query.name);
if (!full.startsWith(base)) return res.status(400).end();
res.sendFile(full);
```

Review this token check. Which three are real weaknesses? (Choose three.)

```js
const SECRET = 'secret';
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, SECRET);   // no options
    next();
  } catch { res.status(401).end(); }
});
```
